-- P5-art-47-48-annex-v: Article 47 (EU declaration of conformity), Article 48 (CE marking) and Annex V (the content of the EU declaration of conformity).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Publications Office consolidation of 27.7.2026 (a plain-text rendering with no legal effect; src:N is its line N).
-- Group: General (Art 113 second paragraph, assumed: keel fork F-113-groups); Annex V takes the group of Article 47, which gives it effect (assumed, not ruled).
-- The Omnibus changed none of Articles 47 and 48 or Annex V (no marker in lines 723 to 736 or 1783 to 1793), so there is one text and no dispatcher on the version.
-- Every provision here is addressed to the provider (or to the provider's authorised representative, or to a notified body, in Article 48(4)): Articles 47 and 48 pass the route, placement date and
-- design change of the one high-risk AI system to the keel's gate, and Art 111(2) may save it (NOTHING). Article 47(5) is a rule-making power (inert, reason 2: NOTES.md).
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE is the text's own yes / no in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered" (NOTES.md).

§ `Article 47: EU declaration of conformity`

DECLARE `Art 47 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 47(1) draw up an EU declaration of conformity`
    `Art 47(1) keep the EU declaration of conformity at the disposal of the national competent authorities`
    `Art 47(1) submit a copy of the EU declaration of conformity to the relevant national competent authorities`
    `Art 47(2) state in the EU declaration of conformity that the high-risk AI system meets the requirements set out in Section 2`
    `Art 47(2) include in the EU declaration of conformity the information set out in Annex V`
    `Art 47(2) translate the EU declaration of conformity into a language that can be easily understood by the national competent authorities`
    `Art 47(3) draw up a single EU declaration of conformity in respect of all Union law applicable to the high-risk AI system`
    `Art 47(4) keep the EU declaration of conformity up-to-date`

§§ `Article 47(1): drawing up, keeping and submitting the declaration`

-- First sentence, first limb. "a written machine readable, physical or electronically signed EU declaration": read as three forms any one of which will do (fork F-47-1-form); a declaration in none of them
-- is not covered by the sentence (NOTHING: the text does not close the list with "only").
-- src:725 | 1. The provider shall draw up a written machine readable, physical or electronically signed EU declaration of conformity for each high-risk AI system, and keep it at the disposal of the national competent authorities for 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service.
@ref Art 47(1) first sentence, first limb (src:725)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 47(1) the provider must draw up an EU declaration of conformity for the high-risk AI system` MEANS
    IF (`Art 40 to 49 Art 2(2) cuts the provision off from the high-risk AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 47 1)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- S14-kind (a list closed by "only"): Article 2(2), "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come, or Art 111(2) saves the system
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:725 | 1. The provider shall draw up a written machine readable, physical or electronically signed EU declaration of conformity for each high-risk AI system, and keep it at the disposal of the national competent authorities for 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service.
@ref Art 47(1) first sentence, the form of the declaration (src:725)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration is written and machine readable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration is physical` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration is electronically signed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 47(1) the declaration is in a form the paragraph names` MEANS
    IF (`Art 40 to 49 Art 2(2) cuts the provision off from the high-risk AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 47 1)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- S14-kind (a list closed by "only"): Article 2(2), "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come, or Art 111(2) saves the system
         ELSE IF `the declaration is written and machine readable` OR `the declaration is physical` OR `the declaration is electronically signed`
