              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sentence names three forms and does not say that no other form will do (fork F-47-1-form)

-- First sentence, second limb: "keep it at the disposal of the national competent authorities for 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service."
-- A period the text fixes in its own words: inside it JUST TRUE; after it JUST FALSE (rule (a) of 2026-11-05). The period is computed from the two dates the function takes, the date asked and the placement date:
-- it runs to the day before the tenth anniversary of the placement date (fork F-47-1-period). A date asked before the placement date is inside it, as it always was: the function has never tested the lower end.
