§ `Annex V: the content of the EU declaration of conformity`

-- The Annex says what the declaration "shall contain": eight points. Points 5 and 7 open with "Where": where the condition fails the point is not required (JUST FALSE, reading (b)). Point 2 ("where applicable, of their
-- authorised representative") and point 4 ("if applicable, with any other relevant Union law") qualify part of a point: the point itself is always required, and the qualified part is the caller's judgment (NOTES.md, Seams).
DECLARE `Annex V point` IS ONE OF
    `Annex V point 1 the AI system name and type and any additional unambiguous reference`
    `Annex V point 2 the name and address of the provider or of the authorised representative`
    `Annex V point 3 a statement that the declaration is issued under the sole responsibility of the provider`
    `Annex V point 4 a statement that the AI system is in conformity with this Regulation and with any other relevant Union law`
    `Annex V point 5 a statement of compliance with the data protection law where personal data is processed`
    `Annex V point 6 references to the harmonised standards or other common specification used`
    `Annex V point 7 the name and identification number of the notified body, the procedure performed and the certificate`
    `Annex V point 8 the place and date of issue, the name and function of the signatory and a signature`

-- src:1785 | The EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47, shall contain all of the following information:
-- src:1786 | 1. AI system name and type and any additional unambiguous reference allowing the identification and traceability of the AI system;
-- src:1787 | 2. The name and address of the provider or, where applicable, of their authorised representative;
-- src:1788 | 3. A statement that the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47 is issued under the sole responsibility of the provider;
-- src:1789 | 4. A statement that the AI system is in conformity with this Regulation and, if applicable, with any other relevant Union law that provides for the issuing of the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47;
-- src:1790 | 5. Where an AI system involves the processing of personal data, a statement that that AI system complies with Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680;
-- src:1791 | 6. References to any relevant harmonised standards used or any other common specification in relation to which conformity is declared;
-- src:1792 | 7. Where applicable, the name and identification number of the notified body, a description of the conformity assessment procedure performed, and identification of the certificate issued;
-- src:1793 | 8. The place and date of issue of the declaration, the name and function of the person who signed it, as well as an indication for, or on behalf of whom, that person signed, a signature.
@ref Annex V (src:1785-1793)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the point of Annex V` IS A `Annex V point`
      `the AI system involves the processing of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notified body was involved in the conformity assessment procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex V the declaration must contain the point` MEANS
    IF (`Art 40 to 49 Art 2(2) cuts the provision off from the high-risk AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 47 0)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- S14-kind (a list closed by "only"): Article 2(2), "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come, or Art 111(2) saves the system
         ELSE CONSIDER `the point of Annex V`
              WHEN `Annex V point 5 a statement of compliance with the data protection law where personal data is processed` THEN
                  IF `the AI system involves the processing of personal data`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an AI system involves the processing of personal data" (a "where" gate: reading (b))
              WHEN `Annex V point 7 the name and identification number of the notified body, the procedure performed and the certificate` THEN
                  IF `a notified body was involved in the conformity assessment procedure`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where applicable" (a "where" gate: reading (b))
              OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref Annex V (src:1785-1793)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the point of Annex V` IS A `Annex V point`
      `the AI system involves the processing of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notified body was involved in the conformity assessment procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 47 act`
`Annex V the provider's duty to include the point in the declaration` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Annex V the declaration must contain the point` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the point of Annex V` `the AI system involves the processing of personal data` `a notified body was involved in the conformity assessment procedure`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN PARTY Provider MUST `Art 47(2) include in the EU declaration of conformity the information set out in Annex V`
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

§ `Article 48: CE marking`

DECLARE `Art 48 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 48(2) use a digital CE marking`
    `Art 48(3) affix the CE marking visibly, legibly and indelibly`
    `Art 48(3) affix the CE marking to the packaging or to the accompanying documentation`
    `Art 48(4) follow the CE marking with the identification number of the notified body`
    `Art 48(4) affix the identification number of the notified body`
    `Art 48(4) indicate the identification number in the promotional material`
    `Art 48(5) indicate in the CE marking that the high-risk AI system also fulfils the requirements of the other Union law`

DECLARE `Art 48(3) place` IS ONE OF
    `Art 48(3) on the high-risk AI system, visibly, legibly and indelibly`
    `Art 48(3) on the packaging`
    `Art 48(3) on the accompanying documentation`

DECLARE `Art 48(4) affixer` IS ONE OF
    `Art 48(4) the notified body itself`
    `Art 48(4) the provider, under the instructions of the notified body`
    `Art 48(4) the provider's authorised representative, under the instructions of the notified body`

§§ `Article 48(1) to (3)`

-- Paragraph 1 points to the general principles of Article 30 of Regulation (EC) No 765/2008, which is not among the sources: the statement that the CE marking is subject to them is encoded, and their content is not.
-- src:732 | 1. The CE marking shall be subject to the general principles set out in Article 30 of Regulation (EC) No 765/2008.
@ref Art 48(1) (src:732)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 48(1) the CE marking is subject to the general principles set out in Article 30 of Regulation (EC) No 765/2008` MEANS
    IF (`Art 40 to 49 Art 2(2) cuts the provision off from the high-risk AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 48 1)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- S14-kind (a list closed by "only"): Article 2(2), "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come, or Art 111(2) saves the system
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- Paragraph 2: "For high-risk AI systems provided digitally, a digital CE marking shall be used, only if it can easily be accessed via the interface from which that system is accessed or via an easily accessible
-- machine-readable code or other electronic means." Read as two propositions (fork F-48-2): a digital CE marking must be used for such a system; and it may be used only if it can easily be accessed in one of the two ways.
-- src:733 | 2. For high-risk AI systems provided digitally, a digital CE marking shall be used, only if it can easily be accessed via the interface from which that system is accessed or via an easily accessible machine-readable code or other electronic means.
@ref Art 48(2) (src:733)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system is provided digitally` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 48(2) a digital CE marking must be used` MEANS
    IF (`Art 40 to 49 Art 2(2) cuts the provision off from the high-risk AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 48 2)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- S14-kind (a list closed by "only"): Article 2(2), "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come, or Art 111(2) saves the system
         ELSE IF `the high-risk AI system is provided digitally`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For high-risk AI systems provided digitally" (a scope limit with no "only")

-- src:733 | 2. For high-risk AI systems provided digitally, a digital CE marking shall be used, only if it can easily be accessed via the interface from which that system is accessed or via an easily accessible machine-readable code or other electronic means.
@ref Art 48(2), the condition (src:733)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system is provided digitally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the digital CE marking can easily be accessed via the interface from which the system is accessed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the digital CE marking can easily be accessed via an easily accessible machine-readable code or other electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 48(2) the digital CE marking may be used` MEANS
    IF (`Art 40 to 49 Art 2(2) cuts the provision off from the high-risk AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 48 2)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- S14-kind (a list closed by "only"): Article 2(2), "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come, or Art 111(2) saves the system
         ELSE IF NOT `the high-risk AI system is provided digitally`
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For high-risk AI systems provided digitally" (a scope limit with no "only")
              ELSE IF `the digital CE marking can easily be accessed via the interface from which the system is accessed` OR `the digital CE marking can easily be accessed via an easily accessible machine-readable code or other electronic means`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if it can easily be accessed via the interface ... or via an easily accessible machine-readable code or other electronic means"

-- Paragraph 3. First sentence: visibly, legibly and indelibly, for high-risk AI systems. Second: "Where that is not possible or not warranted on account of the nature of the high-risk AI system, it shall be affixed
-- to the packaging or to the accompanying documentation, as appropriate." The choice between the two is "as appropriate": a plain input.
-- src:734 | 3. The CE marking shall be affixed visibly, legibly and indelibly for high-risk AI systems. Where that is not possible or not warranted on account of the nature of the high-risk AI system, it shall be affixed to the packaging or to the accompanying documentation, as appropriate.
@ref Art 48(3) (src:734)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `affixing the CE marking to the system is not possible or not warranted on account of the nature of the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the packaging is the appropriate place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Art 48(3) place`
`Art 48(3) where the CE marking must be affixed` MEANS
    IF (`Art 40 to 49 Art 2(2) cuts the provision off from the high-risk AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 48 3)
    THEN NOTHING  -- S14-kind (not a yes or no answer): Article 2(2), "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come, or Art 111(2) saves the system
         ELSE IF NOT `affixing the CE marking to the system is not possible or not warranted on account of the nature of the high-risk AI system`
              THEN JUST `Art 48(3) on the high-risk AI system, visibly, legibly and indelibly`
              ELSE IF `the packaging is the appropriate place`
                   THEN JUST `Art 48(3) on the packaging`
                   ELSE JUST `Art 48(3) on the accompanying documentation`

§§ `Article 48(4) and (5): the notified body's number, and other Union law`

-- First sentence: "Where applicable, the CE marking shall be followed by the identification number of the notified body responsible for the conformity assessment procedures set out in Article 43."
-- Where no notified body is responsible the gate fails: JUST FALSE (reading (b)).
-- src:735 | 4. Where applicable, the CE marking shall be followed by the identification number of the notified body responsible for the conformity assessment procedures set out in Article 43.
